NOTE ON THE CLINICAL CONTENT

The MIT licence covers the source code only. It does not grant any warranty,
and specifically does not certify the clinical accuracy of the Amharic
medical strings in src/i18n/am.json or the fallback answers in src/lib/ai.ts.
The FALLBACK answers are marked NEEDS CLINICIAN REVIEW in the source; the
Amharic medical strings (result.* and assess.*) are not, and are identified
only by the README's before-launch checklist.

The risk model in src/lib/risk.ts and src/lib/regionalRisk.ts is a
transparent weighted model with seeded priors, not measured case rates. A
high-risk verdict is a prompt to seek care, never a diagnosis.

The underlying guidance should stay attributable to WHO and the Ethiopian
Ministry of Health. Cite them; do not restate their protocols as this
app's own.

Anyone deploying this software for use in a clinical setting is responsible
for independent verification by a qualified clinician, and does so at their
own risk.
